window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Proto thought he’d saved the world and found true love. Or at least, he’d achieved some sort of ending, happy or otherwise.</p> <p>So when he wakes up in his bed, right where he’d gone to sleep before arriving at Somnus’ Palace, it’s highly disconcerting. “It really was a dream!” he muses sadly.</p> <p>But, for better or for worse, things are never that simple for Proto. He finds out that what he did back at Somnus’ Palace really was quite important. Overall, he did a good job there as a visitor of dreams, with one exception.</p> <p>Alas, because of that one exception, the world is going to end in a thousand years.</p> <p>Proto already saved the world. Now, he needs to save the future. And the key, it turns out, is his visit to Mercune’s dream.</p> <p>He didn’t get it quite right the first time. Now, he’s got another chance. Will he be able to figure out what he needs to do in Mercune’s dream, in the limited time he has . . . ?</p>"; 
